# A template for Newt's env file under dev (P1.37v; ADR 0030 Decision 2). Every value here is a placeholder. Copy it to
# ../unset-dev-env/newt.env (beside this checkout, 0600, owned by you), then set the real values Pangolin shows when
# the staging site is created; no live env file lives in the checkout. It holds only these three names (preflight
# C31): every other Newt setting is a literal in compose.dev.yaml, which Compose prefers over env_file. The runbook
# docs/human/runbooks/dev-stack-secrets.md says where each value comes from.

# Pangolin's own https address, where Newt dials out.
PANGOLIN_ENDPOINT=replace-me
# The site's id and secret, shown once by Pangolin when the site is created.
NEWT_ID=replace-me
NEWT_SECRET=replace-me
